From 2f209708e4cf21e3364f4efa7f103baa96ea2965 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:03:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 88/99] ++/-- on a bitfield: the result read through the
 bitfield

EX_PREINCDEC stored the new value right but returned its reference with the
bitfield's bits and shift dropped (ExValue(..., 1)), so a read of the
expression's value read the whole storage unit: `if (--p->q)` with
`unsigned q : 6` tested the word that holds q and its neighbours (C89
3.3.3.1: the result is the operand's new value). nethack64's ini_inv(),
"if (--trop->trquan) continue;", never ended. The reference now keeps its
bits and shift.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp b/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp
index ee29855..82e6dbc 100644
--- a/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp
@@ -3410,8 +3410,9 @@ InterCodeGenerator::ExValue InterCodeGenerator::TranslateExpression(Declaration*
 			block->Append(sins);
 #endif
 
-			// Return reference to value
-			return ExValue(vl.mType, vl.mTemp, 1);
+			// Return reference to value: a bitfield's with its bits, or a read of the
+			// result reads the whole storage unit (if (--p->bits) tested the wrong value)
+			return ExValue(vl.mType, vl.mTemp, 1, vl.mBits, vl.mShift);
 		}
 		break;
 
